# Google ADK agents

Use **Google ADK** (`google.adk`) to build agents — not LangChain, CrewAI, or custom agent loops unless explicitly requested.

## Agent definition

- Define agents with `Agent` from `google.adk.agents`
- Tools are plain Python functions (not tool classes)
- Keep instructions, model name, and tool lists explicit and readable
- Put agent modules in the owning microservice (or a dedicated AI service); keep eval harnesses separate
- Do not import another service's agent internals — expose capabilities via that service's API

```python
# ✅ GOOD
from google.adk.agents import Agent

root_agent = Agent(
    model=TEXT_MODEL,
    name="booking_agent",
    description="Helps users search and manage bookings.",
    instruction="You are a booking assistant...",
    tools=[search_availability, create_booking],
)
```

## Runtime

- Execute with ADK `Runner` + session services
- Use `InMemorySessionService` only for local/dev; prefer durable session storage (e.g. Postgres) for real deployments
- Expose agents to clients via FastAPI routes/WebSockets — don't bury HTTP in agent modules

## Config & secrets

- Model IDs and voice settings via env (`GOOGLE_API_KEY`, `TEXT_MODEL`, etc.)
- Never hardcode API keys
- Keep prompts/instructions versioned in code or dedicated prompt modules under `ai/`
